---
import { deskEquipment } from '../../lib/content';
---

<div id="tech" class="content-section">
  <span id="tab-tech" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <h2 class="section-title">HomeOffice</h2>
  <section class="homeoffice-section" aria-labelledby="desk-setup-heading">
    <h3 id="desk-setup-heading">Desk Setup</h3>
    <div class="table-wrapper">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Category</th>
            <th>Equipment</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {deskEquipment.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{row.data.category}</td>
              <td>{row.data.equipment}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="links-grid">
      <div class="link-item">
        <a href="https://vsco.co/attaboyabhi/media/65c395b793559a0b87ef31b8">
          Desk Setup 1
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="link-item">
        <a href="https://vsco.co/attaboyabhi/media/66d892fdcb549a1437fac762">
          Desk Setup 2
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="homeoffice-section" aria-labelledby="unifi-heading">
    <h3 id="unifi-heading">UniFi</h3>
    <p>
      A <strong>UniFi Cloud Gateway Fiber</strong> handles routing, security,
      and centralised network management. My <strong>U7 Pro XGS</strong> access
      point provides Wi-Fi 7 coverage across approximately 1,650 sq ft,
      positioned centrally to reach through concrete internal walls and powered
      by a dedicated 90W PoE injector.
    </p>
    <p>
      UniFi brings client, traffic, and Wi-Fi monitoring into one place, with
      remote administration and Teleport VPN access when away. There is room to
      add UniFi Protect cameras and more PoE devices.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="homeoffice-section" aria-labelledby="synology-nas-heading">
    <h3 id="synology-nas-heading">Synology NAS Setup</h3>
    <p>
      My <strong>Synology DiskStation DS1621+</strong> doubles as an always-on
      home server. This 6-bay NAS runs on an AMD Ryzen V1500B, with roughly{' '}
      <strong>31 TB of storage</strong> across multiple pools, disk redundancy,
      and <strong>10GbE networking</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Alongside centralised storage and backups, it has hosted Homebridge,
      Synology Drive, and containers through Synology Container Manager, with
      SSH for administration. It also serves as a platform for experimenting
      with data-engineering workloads, including evaluating Airbyte in
      containers or virtual machines.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
